Q.1 Explain the difference between frontend, backend, and full-stack development with suitable real-world examples?
Ans. 
Frontend: The part users see and interact with, built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
Example: The product page and buttons on Amazon.

Backend: The server-side that manages data and logic using languages like Node.js or Python.
Example: Saving items to your Amazon cart.

Full-Stack: Works on both frontend and backend.
Example: A developer handling both the Amazon interface and order system.
