Q.3 Describe how a browser requests and displays a web page from a web server?
Ans.
When you enter a website URL, the browser sends an "HTTP request" to the web server. The server processes the request, retrieves the required files (HTML, CSS, JavaScript), and sends them back. The browser then "renders"" these files to display the web page on your screen.

