Q.4 Identify and list the tools required to set up a web development environment? Explain the purpose of each!
Ans.
Code Editor (e.g., VS Code): Used to write and edit code efficiently.
Web Browser (e.g., Chrome): To test and preview web pages.
Version Control (e.g., Git): Tracks code changes and manages versions.
Package Manager (e.g., npm): Installs and manages libraries or dependencies.
Local Server (e.g., XAMPP, Node.js): Runs and tests web applications locally.
Frameworks/Libraries (e.g., React, Bootstrap): Speeds up design and development.

